 "about": "An independent re-digitization of figure-read curves by a different method: the figure PDF is rendered to a 400 dpi raster, the axes are recalibrated from tick marks found in the raster, and the curve is traced by colour; the vector paths the original extraction used are never read. Curves were drawn at random (seeded random stream, seed 20261018, from the 744 digitized simulation records with a figure PDF at the time) until 20 could be checked. A curve passes if its largest difference from the stored values is within max(0.02 dex on a log axis, 1.5 pixels at 400 dpi). A curve that fails is not necessarily wrong: each failure was looked at and attributed to the check (a marker, error bar or other curve of the same colour on top of the stroke) or called inconclusive. This is not a verdict on the 76 curves that could not be checked (overlapping same-colour curves, raster or outlined axes, quantities stored after a transform).",
